<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariano Guadalupe Vallejo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1807">1807</a>–<a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mariano Guadalupe Vallejo was a Californio military commander and landowner, comandante of the northern frontier of Mexican Alta <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, where he laid out the town of Sonoma in 1835. Rebels of the Bear Flag revolt seized him at Sonoma in June 1846 and held him prisoner for several weeks. He later sat in California's constitutional convention and its first state senate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariano-guadalupe-vallejo.jpg" alt="Mariano Guadalupe Vallejo" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I. W. Taber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariano_Guadalupe_Vallejo_Oval.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
